From dbea13d3403c00c815436097359b8e8116491075 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Deniz Kokden <koekdendeniz@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 11:45:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] android: camera_device: Set camera usage in the mapping
 stream builder

gralloc picks the actual format of IMPLEMENTATION_DEFINED streams from
their usage. buildStreamConfigsNoMap() therefore marks every stream as
written by the camera, the mapping builder only JPEG streams, so the
preview buffers became XBGR8888 instead of NV12 and the buffer import
failed. Mark the other streams the same way.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
Change-Id: Iafaa98a6ed8c1c72910802f514141bc1cae2ca72
---
 src/android/camera_device.cpp | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/android/camera_device.cpp b/src/android/camera_device.cpp
index 9dac3bcd..b3f46d01 100644
--- a/src/android/camera_device.cpp
+++ b/src/android/camera_device.cpp
@@ -260,6 +260,15 @@ bool isJpegStream(camera3_stream_t *stream)
 			continue;
 		}
 
+		/*
+		 * As in buildStreamConfigsNoMap(): gralloc picks the actual
+		 * format of IMPLEMENTATION_DEFINED from the usage, so mark
+		 * every stream as written by the camera.
+		 */
+		stream->usage |= (GRALLOC_USAGE_HW_CAMERA_WRITE |
+				  GRALLOC_USAGE_SW_READ_OFTEN |
+				  GRALLOC_USAGE_SW_WRITE_OFTEN);
+
 		/*
 		 * If a CameraStream with the same size and format as the
 		 * current stream has already been requested, associate the two.
-- 
